---
import ResourceGuide from "../ResourceGuide.astro";
import ResourceGuideHero from "../ResourceGuideHero.astro";
---

<ResourceGuide>
  <ResourceGuideHero title="Accelerator application guide">
      <p class="guide-lead mt-6">To prepare an accelerator application, check the program&#x27;s eligibility, explain what your company does, support your claims with measured results, and introduce your founding team. Follow the current application form&#x27;s instructions for written answers and video.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">This guide combines 886 Studios&#x27; application advice with current ikigai Launchpad program details. It is a preparation checklist, not an application form or a statement that applications are open.</p>
      <a class="guide-hero__cta mt-7 btn-pri" href="#checklist">Use the checklist</a>
      <nav aria-label="In this guide" class="guide-contents mt-9">
        <a href="#program-fit" class="guide-link">Program fit</a>
        <a href="#application-answers" class="guide-link">Written answers</a>
        <a href="#intro-video" class="guide-link">Introduction video</a>
        <a href="#application-faq" class="guide-link">Application FAQs</a>
      </nav>
  </ResourceGuideHero>
  <section class="guide-checklist" id="checklist">
    <div class="guide-container">
      <h2>Before you apply</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Before you apply to an accelerator, make sure you are prepared to join one. Go through this checklist and ask yourself some questions.</p>
      <div class="guide-stack mt-9">
        <div class="guide-checklist__item">
          <h3>Do you have a cofounder?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Some accelerators prioritize startups with a cofounder. If you don’t have one, begin to plan how you might get one and brainstorm what you would look for in a cofounder.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-checklist__item">
          <h3>Is your LinkedIn professional?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Accelerators and potential investors do check your LinkedIn. Be authentic and transparent about work experience, technical skills, and portfolio. Keep photos and language professional.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-checklist__item">
          <h3>Has your resume been updated?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Make sure your resume is up to date with the projects you are currently working on. This makes it easier for accelerators to track your professional timeline.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-checklist__item">
          <h3>Are you working full-time on this startup?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Accelerators are looking for dedication from founders. Ask yourself how much time you currently spend on your company and whether other work may be distracting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-checklist__item">
          <h3>Can you communicate your pitch well?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Be prepared for questions in English. It is helpful to send a pre-read before meetings, use slides and graphics wisely, and practice the flow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-checklist__item">
          <h3>What do you hope to gain from the program?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Different programs fit different industries and stages. Consider whether you want mentors, demo day practice, community, rigorous coursework, or other outcomes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-checklist__qualification mt-7">For ikigai Launchpad, a co-founder is not required. Solo founders can apply, but the founding team needs credible technical or domain capability. <a class="guide-link" href="/ikigai-launchpad">Read the program requirements</a> before deciding whether it fits your team.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-fit" id="program-fit">
    <div class="guide-container">
      <h2>Choose a program that fits</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">After going through the checklist, you may decide to apply to an accelerator. Depending on your company stage, industry, and timeline, the program you choose should fit your startup needs.</p>
      <p class="mt-5">Compare each program&#x27;s stage, location, time commitment, investment terms, and support. For an overview of local options, use the <a href="/resources/ecosystem-database" class="guide-link">Taiwan startup ecosystem database</a>.</p>
      <div class="guide-fit__program mt-7">
        <h3>What is ikigai Launchpad?</h3>
        <p class="mt-3">ikigai Launchpad is 886 Studios&#x27; 10-week, in-person accelerator in Taipei for early-stage founders building for a global market. Founders can apply from anywhere and should be working full-time, or ready to do so. All co-founders are expected to join on site for the core program.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">ikigai Launchpad&#x27;s standard investment is $100,000 USD for 8% through a SAFE. There is no additional program fee. These terms are stated on the <a href="/ikigai-launchpad" class="guide-link">ikigai Launchpad program page</a>.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">The next batch is Spring 2027. Application dates and the deadline have not been announced. Check the <a href="/ikigai-launchpad" class="guide-link">current program page</a> for the latest timing and terms. This application checklist is preparation guidance, not a statement that applications are open.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">Looking for workspace and a founder community rather than an accelerator investment? <a href="/launch-station" class="guide-link">Launch Station</a> is a separate, invitation-only, 90-day builder residency in Taipei with no cost or equity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-answers" id="application-answers">
    <div class="guide-container">
      <h2>Write clear application answers</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Accelerators get pitched many interesting startups with a lot of potential. If the person reading your application can’t understand the concept based on your explanation, they may pass. Knowing how to answer application questions is a valuable skill.</p>
      <div class="guide-stack mt-7">
        <div class="guide-answers__item">
          <h3>The STAR method</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">For behavioral or personal questions, organize your answer around situation, task, action, and result. Keep the situation and task short, spend the most time on your actions, and reflect on what happened and what you learned.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-answers__item">
          <h3>Be straightforward</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">When a question asks a simple “what,” do not add filler or marketing-speak. Add detail only when it is relevant and necessary.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-answers__item">
          <h3>Use honest numbers</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Be truthful with market size, runway, revenue, expenses, and other metrics. Accelerators may check your data and ask how you calculated it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-answers__item">
          <h3>Explain the competition</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Do not claim you have no competition. Competition can be any alternative a customer uses. We care more about your plan to overcome obstacles than an unrealistic claim that none exist.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6">Before you submit, ask someone unfamiliar with your company to read the application. Can they describe the customer, the problem, and what you are building? Replace any claim they cannot understand with a specific explanation. Keep forecasts separate from results you have already measured.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-video" id="intro-video">
    <div class="guide-container">
      <h2>Prepare your introduction video</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">Many accelerator applications ask for a short introduction video describing your team and startup. The goal is clarity, not production value.</p>
      <p class="mt-4">If a one-minute video is requested, use the checklist below. Follow the current form&#x27;s length and upload instructions if they differ.</p>
      <ul class="guide-list mt-6">
        <li>Keep the video to one minute.</li>
        <li>Upload it to YouTube, allow embedding, and mark it as unlisted if needed.</li>
        <li>Make sure the audio quality is clear.</li>
        <li>Try not to read from a script; it should sound like a face-to-face conversation.</li>
        <li>Make explanations simple and easy to understand.</li>
        <li>Make sure all co-founders are included.</li>
        <li>Do not add special effects or background music.</li>
        <li>Do not use the video as a full product demo. Explain the team’s passion, why this idea, and why this journey.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-faq" id="application-faq">
    <div class="guide-container">
      <h2>Application FAQs</h2>
      <div class="guide-questions mt-8">
        <div id="application-preparation" class="guide-anchor">
          <h3>What should I prepare for accelerator applications?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Prepare a clear company description, current founder profiles and resumes, measured business results, and an explanation of why the accelerator fits your team. If a founder video is requested, follow that application&#x27;s length and upload instructions. Each accelerator sets its own requirements; this preparation guide does not replace its application form.</p>
          <p class="guide-faq__answer-source mt-3">Read <span><a class="guide-link" href="#application-answers">886 Studios&#x27; written-answer guidance</a></span>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="founder-eligibility" class="guide-anchor">
          <h3>Can I apply to ikigai Launchpad without a co-founder or company entity?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Yes. ikigai Launchpad accepts solo founders, and no incorporated entity is required to apply. The founding team still needs credible technical or domain capability. If accepted, founders will typically need to establish a US entity to receive funding. These are ikigai Launchpad&#x27;s requirements, not rules for every accelerator.</p>
          <p class="guide-faq__answer-source mt-3">Read <span><a class="guide-link" href="/ikigai-launchpad">ikigai Launchpad&#x27;s eligibility FAQ</a></span>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="international-founders" class="guide-anchor">
          <h3>Can international founders apply to ikigai Launchpad?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Yes. ikigai Launchpad is open to founders from anywhere. The 10-week core program takes place in person in Taipei, and all co-founders are expected to join on site. Founders should be working full-time, or ready to work full-time, and able to attend the batch in Taipei.</p>
          <p class="guide-faq__answer-source mt-3">Read <span><a class="guide-link" href="/ikigai-launchpad">ikigai Launchpad&#x27;s attendance and eligibility details</a></span>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="application-timing" class="guide-anchor">
          <h3>When can I apply to the next ikigai Launchpad batch?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">The next ikigai Launchpad batch is Spring 2027. As of October 12, 2026, application dates and the deadline have not been announced on the program page. Check that page for updated timing before submitting; this guide does not confirm that applications are open.</p>
          <p class="guide-faq__answer-source mt-3">Read <span><a class="guide-link" href="/ikigai-launchpad">ikigai Launchpad&#x27;s application timeline</a></span>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="business-metrics" class="guide-anchor">
          <h3>What business numbers should I prepare for an accelerator interview?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">886 Studios&#x27; Interview Guidebook asks founders to prepare monthly operating expenses, runway, previous funding, and user or revenue metrics if applicable. Be ready to explain how you calculated each figure. Report measured results honestly and keep forecasts separate from results you have already achieved.</p>
          <p class="guide-faq__answer-source mt-3">Read <span><a class="guide-link" href="/interview-guidebook">886 Studios&#x27; Interview Guidebook</a></span><span> and <a class="guide-link" href="#application-answers">the written-answer guidance</a></span>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="interview-format" class="guide-anchor">
          <h3>Do I need a pitch deck for the first ikigai Launchpad interview?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">No. The first ikigai Launchpad interview is a 20-minute conversation with the 886 Studios team. You don’t need a pitch deck. Come ready to discuss your team, the problem you’re solving, what you’re building, your progress, and what you’ve learned from users. Prepare questions for the team, too.</p>
          <p class="guide-faq__answer-source mt-3">Read <span><a class="guide-link" href="/ikigai-launchpad">ikigai Launchpad&#x27;s interview FAQ</a></span><span> and <a class="guide-link" href="/interview-guidebook">the Interview Guidebook</a></span>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="guide-faq__sources mt-7">Prepared by 886 Studios. Program source page checked on <time datetime="2026-10-12">October 12, 2026</time>. First interview guidance updated on <time datetime="2026-10-14">October 14, 2026</time>. Follow the current program page and your interview invitation if their instructions change.</p>
      <div class="guide-next mt-10">
        <h2>Check your next step</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Review the current program details and application timing before you apply. Use the preparation checklist now so your answers are ready when the next application window is announced.</p>
        <a class="mt-6 btn-pri" href="/ikigai-launchpad">Review the program</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ResourceGuide>
